tructure and Consolidation
Create a "One-Slider": Condense the core message from multiple slides into a single, high-level summary slide.

Move Details to the Appendix: Place the current, detailed slides into the appendix so they are available if anyone wants to "drill down" into the specifics.

Keep the API Slide: Maintain one dedicated slide specifically for the API landscape and requirements.

Content Requirements for the Main Slide
The single summary slide needs to be structured around four key blocks:

What: What exactly is wanted.

Why: Why it is needed.

How: How it will be implemented.

Outcome: What the final output or benefit will be.

Additionally, ensure this main slide clearly calls out the benefits, specifically breaking them down into:

Your Benefit: Centralized visibility and license management for Workday (e.g., scheduled data refreshes).

Organizational Benefit: Optimization opportunities, such as user device tagging and tracking leavers/movers.
